{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And he turned aside to her toward the road.</b> From the way she was — he turned aside to the way she was in; דשטורנ\"יר בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>Come now.</b> Prepare yourself and your mind for this. Every expression of הָבָה is an expression of preparation, except in a place where it can be rendered as an expression of giving — and even those of preparation are close to the expression of giving."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French destourner, 'to turn aside/away'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:38.528570731Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}